+## 10. AI Provenance Logging Is Mandatory
+
+*(Added 2026-09-06)*
+
+Every AI model that completes a task in this archive must log the completion in `methodology/ai_provenance.md` before marking the task DONE. This is a universal rule, not a list of named tools — model names change, get renamed, get deprecated. Any current or future agent onboards through `README_FOR_EXTERNAL_AGENTS.md`, which points here.
+
+The log exists so that:
+- Any later agent or human can trace which model's reasoning produced a given change, instead of an anonymous commit.
+- If that reasoning later turns out to be wrong, the failure is traceable to a specific entry — not lost.
+- Patterns in where different models' logic tends to break down become visible over time, instead of each model repeating the same blind spot.
+
+A task is not complete without a provenance entry. An entry that later proves wrong is never deleted — the correction goes in `CORRECTIONS.md` with a link back to it, per Law 4 (No Algorithmic Contamination): errors are logged and held on record, never quietly erased.
+
+**Interrupted tasks:** if a model is cut off mid-task (session limit, timeout, quota), it logs a partial entry with status `IN PROGRESS`, documenting what was done and what remains. The next model picks up from that entry — not from scratch.
+
+---
+
