+# AI Provenance Log
+
+**Purpose:** Track which AI model completed which task, when, and under what reasoning — so any future agent or Wendy can trace a change back to the model that made it, check whether that model's logic still holds, and log a fix if it doesn't.
+**Companion files:** `decision_log.md` (framework decisions), `CORRECTIONS.md` (errors caught after the fact)
+**Applies to:** every AI model working in this archive. See `README_FOR_EXTERNAL_AGENTS.md`.
+
+---
+
+## How to Use This File
+
+When any task in `TASK_QUEUE.md` is marked DONE, the completing model appends an entry here before moving on. Entries are **append-only** — never edit or delete a prior entry, even your own.
+
+If a later session finds an earlier entry's reasoning was wrong, the correction goes in `CORRECTIONS.md`, with a link back to the entry number here. The entry itself stays on record. This mirrors Law 4 (No Algorithmic Contamination): errors are logged and held on record, never quietly erased.
+
+## Entry Format
+
+```
+### PROV-XXX: [Task name]
+- **Task:** [Task # from TASK_QUEUE.md]
+- **Completed by:** [Model name + version]
+- **Date:** YYYY-MM-DD
+- **What was done:** [1-3 sentences]
+- **Reasoning / assumptions made:** [anything a future reader should sanity-check]
+- **Files touched:** [list]
+- **Flag for re-check:** [Yes/No — did this rely on a judgment call rather than a hard rule?]
+```
+
+---
+
