+## 6. Search Documentation Standards
+
+*(Added 2026-09-06)*
+
+### 6.1 Search Completeness Rule
+
+Every `.md` page in `/people/` and `/research_queue/` must maintain a Search Log documenting which tools searched which record types, what was found, and what was NOT searched. A tool that searches one category and doesn't document categories it didn't search has introduced bias by omission. The ❌ NOT SEARCHED tag is an honest map of where to go next, not a failure.
+
+Format (full page template in `TASK_QUEUE.md` Task 4):
+
+`Date | Tool/Agent | What was searched | What was found | What was NOT searched`
+
+### 6.2 Search Direction Bias Check
+
+Before publishing any "Where To Look Next" recommendation — on a `/people/` page, in `/research_queue/`, or on a public-facing page (`contribute.html`, `analysis.html`, `context.html`) — the recommendation must be checked against this question: what record types exist that this agent might not know to suggest? What would a Narragansett historian, a maritime historian, an archaeologist, a linguist, or a material-culture specialist look for that a genealogist wouldn't?
+
+If the recommendation is entirely digitized, English-language, colonial-framework sources, it has not passed this check. Flag the gap explicitly rather than presenting the list as thorough.
+
+---
+
+*See `methodology/ai_provenance.md` PROV-001 for authorship and reasoning.*
